<br/>
<br/>The Timeless Isle, this time around, will effectively function as a way to get enough iLvl to step into Celestials.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_offhand_ulduarraid_d_03.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Combat Rogue Pre-Raid Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>
<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Combat Rogues should typically use two passive trinkets, and sometimes one on-use and one passive, but rarely ever two on-use. In the case of Phase 5 of Mists of Pandaria, we will default to our two standard passive trinkets.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<br/>There are no active trinkets of note worth mentioning for Combat Rogues, as all of our strongest trinkets are Passive Trinkets.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=104974/assurance-of-consequence">
<img alt="Assurance of Consequence" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_14.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Assurance of Consequence</span></a> is by far our best trinket option for all three rogue specializations. The Celestial version, lowering your major ability CDs by 35%, is an extremely powerful effect both defensively and offensively.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105029/haromms-talisman">
<img alt="Haromm's Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haromm's Talisman</span></a> is our second-best trinket for single-target DPS for all three specializations. Multistriking + a large agility proc is exactly what we want during our CDs.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105082/sigil-of-rampage">
<img alt="Sigil of Rampage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sigil of Rampage</span></a> is the worst trinket for single-target DPS from our available options. The cleave proc makes it uniquely good for multi-target encounters.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105114/ticking-ebon-detonator">
<img alt="Ticking Ebon Detonator" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_17.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ticking Ebon Detonator</span></a> is our least desired trinket option, as it provides less AoE throughput than Sigil of Rampage and less single-target than Haromm's Talisman. Though it isn't a horrible option if you can't get hold of either.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="legendary-cloak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_theblackprince.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Legendary Cloak for Combat Rogue</span></h2>With the removal of Raid Finder in Mists of Pandaria Classic, it is possible to earn your Legendary Cloak without ever setting foot into a raid.  This can be done inside Celestial Dungeons.<br/>
<br/>Finally, we're able to acquire <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102248/fen-yu-fury-of-xuen">
<img alt="Fen-Yu, Fury of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_tigermelee_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fen-Yu, Fury of Xuen</span></a>. This cloak's proc is great for cleave and single target. The procs per minute will vary slightly depending on whether you're Subtlety, Combat, or Assassination, with Combat's expected PPM (procs per minute) to be 2.00 + Haste.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
