<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Combat Rogues</span></span></h2>
<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>Crafted items are no longer restricted by your Profession option, except for Engineering, so this allows us to equip Leatherworking items without Leatherworking if we need to.<br/>
<br/>MoP's final patch comes with two new iLvl 553 crafted pieces. Both of these will be a bit expensive, but if you're getting unlucky, they'll hold you over until you receive loot from the raid.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98613/snow-lily-belt">
<img alt="Snow Lily Belt" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_leather_panprog_b_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Snow Lily Belt</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98604/snow-lily-britches">
<img alt="Snow Lily Britches" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pant_leather_panprog_b_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Snow Lily Britches</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Combat Rogues</span></span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit or 2550 Hit Rating and 7.5% Expertise or 2550 Expertise Rating. Keep in mind that some abilities such as racial weapon expertise will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer miss dungeon or raid bosses. Our Poisons are now also based off the melee hit table, meaning that 7.5% is all that it takes to ensure that our Poisons never miss. Your regular swings (white damage) still have a chance to miss until the dual-wield Hit cap of 26.5%. This is calculated by taking the base miss chance of 3%, adding the dual-wield penalty of 19%, then adding 1.5% per level above you the enemy is, for a total cap of 26.5%.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, bosses will no longer be able to dodge your attacks. They will, however, still be able to parry them when attacked from the front. For the vast majority of bosses, you will be positioned behind them, and enemies cannot parry attacks from behind.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Gemming for Combat Rogues</span></span></h2>Gemming is fairly straightforward throughout Mists of Pandaria. You look to get as much Agility as possible and tend to make socket bonus choices based if they will give you more Agility or equal Agility with additional secondary stats. The new <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> arrives in Phase 3. It'll require you to kill bosses in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a> and acquire 20 <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94593/secrets-of-the-empire">
<img alt="Secrets of the Empire" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/secrets_of_the_empire_icon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Secrets of the Empire</span></a>, as well as 40 <a class="q2 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=72095/trillium-bar">
<img alt="Trillium Bar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ingot_trillium.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Trillium Bar</span></a>. This new gem brings the buff <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=137596/capacitance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_purge.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitance</span></a>. The PPM for different specializations varies quite a bit.<br/>
<br/>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
